  "Number": 6,
  "Question": "\\(AB\\) is a diameter of a circle centered at \\(O.\\) \\(C\\) is a point on the circle such that angle \\(BOC\\) is \\(60^\\circ.\\) If the diameter of the circle is \\(5\\) inches, the length of chord \\(AC,\\) expressed in inches, is:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(3\\)",
    "B": "\\(\\dfrac{5\\sqrt2}{2}\\)",
    "C": "\\(\\dfrac{5\\sqrt3}{2}\\)",
    "D": "\\(3\\sqrt3\\)",
    "E": "none of these"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "The radius is \\(5/2\\) inches, so \\(OB=OC=5/2\\). Thus triangle \\(BOC\\) is isosceles. Its vertex angle is \\(60^\\circ\\), so its other two angles are also \\(60^\\circ\\). It is equilateral, giving\n\\[\nBC=\\frac52.\n\\]\nBecause \\(AB\\) is a diameter and \\(C\\) lies on the circle, \\(\\angle ACB=90^\\circ\\). This makes \\(AB=5\\) the hypotenuse of right triangle \\(ABC\\). By the Pythagorean theorem,\n\\[\nAC^2=AB^2-BC^2\n=25-\\frac{25}{4}\n=\\frac{75}{4}.\n\\]\nTaking the positive square root, since \\(AC\\) is a length, gives \\(\\boxed{AC=\\dfrac{5\\sqrt3}{2}}\\) inches, choice \\(\\mathrm C\\).",
